{"title":"1992 AHSME Problems/Problem 15","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AHSME_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/9/75952e52a3dc061d24146c0df9062a54a5ce5a5e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i=\\sqrt{-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"71\" height=\"21\" />. Define a sequence of complex numbers by\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/3/453863d57253cb6e8dabf7f2f486b89f70402788.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[z_1=0,\\quad z_{n+1}=z_{n}^2+i \\text{ for } n\\ge1.\\]\" width=\"256\" height=\"19\" />\nIn the complex plane, how far from the origin is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/2/7828d9bb7fa3588d4d2c473376bc895a5ac1681e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_{111}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"27\" height=\"10\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/f/e8f3d73c929ffd1f4b7e0efe9a2658d63309ff06.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A) } 1\\quad \\text{(B) } \\sqrt{2}\\quad \\text{(C) } \\sqrt{3}\\quad \\text{(D) } \\sqrt{110}\\quad \\text{(E) } \\sqrt{2^{55}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"357\" height=\"21\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AHSME_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/c/13c3218ca790f4eac4048f34f68433655b19e1f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\fbox{B}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"23\" height=\"23\" /> Write out some terms: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/d/50d24e82f197284193560e9289b54f172421cd58.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0, i, -1+i, -i, -1+i, -i, -1+i, -i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"287\" height=\"16\" />, etc., and it keeps alternating between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/b/0cb4b0b774fad5fd161d1d5a8046eeb29f114db6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1+i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/d/0fda51aabf3fa68a72ba3b46518abc175c76dab2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-i$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" />, so as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/d/58d1eed7be2e1dcbfd4f7fe86fba2eb7566d8bbf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$111$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> is odd, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/2/7828d9bb7fa3588d4d2c473376bc895a5ac1681e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_{111}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"27\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/b/0cb4b0b774fad5fd161d1d5a8046eeb29f114db6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1+i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />. Thus its distance from the origin is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/f/abfc2f98cf9999aa2fa2052995d0097c50497140.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{(-1)^2+1^2} = \\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"152\" height=\"35\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AHSME_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;tex